A||||13||LZeitgeist||Pics of our latest project - the 1988 Indy II... ||||7||
Z||000000||LZeitgeist||03-24-2001||06:57 PM||||Here 'tis... we started out with my old red 1988 Coupe, added the nose, tail and ground effects from a junkyard '87 GT, traded some leftover parts for a wing, painted the car and the wheels white, painted the ground effects metallic medium grey, added the various decals and such, finished it off with a red gradiated stripe kit from Phoenix Graphix, and voila...<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagemethos/DadsCar1"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagemethos/DadsCar2">  <P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/bronzeagemethos/DadsCar3">  <P>I had made door decals for it that looked official, but had changed them to '72nd Indianapolis 500', and 'May 1988' (we're not trying to fool anybody into thinking it's an original '84 - one look at the decklid will tell you that - but we saw a real Indy up in Virgina last year and fell in love with it - and the idea for our project was born...), but we decided that the black door lettering would be overkill for this project (although we like the way it looks on the real Indys)...<P>The interior is still a long way from 'show quality', but we'll be working on that next...<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Songman||03-24-2001||07:03 PM||||Looks like what I have planned for my 88 coupe too... Except I plan to have a 3800SC under the deck with a 4T60E 4-speed automatic. Still toying with the idea of a fastback. May be even trading my 88 coupe for an 87 T-top car. And I am also going for the wheels, white moulding, and lighted air scoop like on the track version! <P>Like you, not building it to try to fool anyone. I don't even want it to look like a real Indy. Doing it for a couple of reasons. 1) Don't want to do any mods to my real Indy. 2) Gives me something that I can drive all the time, since I won't the real Indy. 3) Will be cool at car shows to have my real Indy, my NASCAR Aerocoupe Monte Carlo, and my hopped up Indy Clone.<P>Great looking car you've got there!! And I like the Indy II idea!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||03-24-2001||07:04 PM||||BTW... this car has the original 4-cyl. engine still in it, still going strong with over 252,000 miles on it, and no internal engine work ever needing to be done (knock on wood)... <P>We even put the red stripes on the rims... *that* was fun, let me tell you... (Personally, I'd prefer to put white-painted diamondspoke rims on it with the proper '88 offsets, to highlight that it is, in fact, an '88, but Dad likes these rims better... but, someday it will be mine again, and I'll swap the rims over then.)<P>Also BTW, that's my red Formula in the backgound of the second shot up there... damn, Dad's car is more eye-catching than mine now! Can't have that!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||03-24-2001||07:06 PM||||Oh, we also hung onto the V6 and 5-speed tranny from the '87 GT.. when the 4-cyl. gives up the ghost, it it will go... a V6-powered Indy, just like it should have been!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||03-24-2001||07:22 PM||||Looks good.<P>If I decide to keep it, I'm planning similar with my '86SE. But, instead, will paint it black with silver skirts, leave shiny silver 14" tech wheels on, put on the Indy decklid decal, red stripes, etc, but put white indy door decals on. It won't fool any Fiero person into thinking it is real, and it will be my Indy. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||03-24-2001||08:21 PM||||I,m not sure where(?), but I saw a GT dressed as an Indy . Very pretty!||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||03-25-2001||07:40 PM||||Thanks for the compliments, gang... glad you like it... I know we can't stop looking at it, thinking "Wow... *we* did that??"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||03-25-2001||08:53 PM||||And best of all, it RUNS!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000008||danny boy||03-25-2001||10:57 PM||||I've got an Idea for you.Use FWD rims on the front to get closer to the '88 offset.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Kelvin Vivian||03-26-2001||04:05 AM||||That is one NICE Indy Fiero clone... I've always liked the color scheme of the Indy Fiero and white 85 GTs.  <P>An 88 coupe to an Indy Fiero... sounds like a fun project!<P>What would tip me off that it might not be a true Indy would be the following:<P>1. The missing debossed "Pontiac" in the rear facia.<BR>2. Although I can't see it in the picture, an 88 should have a third brake light, and 84's didn't have one.<BR>3. No dual exhaust.<BR>4. The '72 Indianapolis door decal would also be a good hint...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Great job...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=1&res=high">   88 T-top, 5-spd & 87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||03-26-2001||07:12 AM||||danny boy - <BR>That's an excellent idea... do you know off the top of your head which rims would work? '88 Sunbird, maybe?<P>If it were mine, I'd do it, but Dad doesn't want to be hassled with different wheel/tire sizes front and rear... (I'm glad he doesn't own a Formula, then.) He would rather stick to the old-school way or tire rotation, etc. &lt;bleah&gt;<P>(Of course, if it was mine, I'd have white-painted Formula rims on it anyway, but I digress...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P><BR>Kelvin - <BR>Yup, it was fun. Much work, but fun. Still have the interior to restore, if I can keep Dad from just drilling holes for switches into whatever panel is handy and putting screws wherever he sees something coming loose... *sigh* I love him, but he's past the age where interior aesthetics are in his calculations for car repairs. Argh. <P>I hadn't thought about the rear 'Pontiac'... good eye...<P>Being an '88, it does have a third brake light. Won't pass NC state inspection without one if it's '86 or newer.<P>We haven't done any engine work to it, so it won't acquire the dual exhaust until we put the V6 in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>We taped the 72nd Indy decal to the door, but it just looked like we were trying too hard to prove something with it... we didn't make the clone to fool anybody, just to have the best of both worlds.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Excellent observations... <P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||TheFiero64||03-26-2001||07:13 PM||||I've always wanted to make an Indy fastback. Here is one I saw at Rutland MA. (my red 88 is behind it.)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gas.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000012||danny boy||03-26-2001||08:07 PM|||| sunbird wheels should work.They came on Grand Ams,too.I'm sure they came on other cars but I'm not sure which ones.They are EVERYWHERE around here,so they should not be hard to find.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||03-27-2001||02:47 PM||||Cool - thanks for the idea... I'll bounce it off Dad and see if he wants to go for it...||||reg||1
